  "id": "Unheard.usec",
  "description": "Ports patch_tplprofile's THICC/SICC/etc hideout-slot injection from patch.ts. Original code cloned an *existing* hideout-slotted item to copy its parentId/location shape and stamped a fresh random _id per run; a static JSON patch can't call a function, so '_id' values below are fixed placeholders (690000000000000000000001..0e) and 'parentId' is a fixed value - both verified against the live Unheard.usec template via tools/check_hideout_ids.py (parentId=664115f68b8ae85875060b39, confirmed the single value actually used there; no _id collisions found). Re-run that script after any templates/profiles.json update before re-enabling, in case the parentId changed. Original guarded with 'if not already added' because it rewrote the JSON file on disk and would otherwise duplicate on every re-run; this engine instead re-patches a fresh in-memory copy of the template every server boot (nothing is written back to templates/profiles.json), so the plain 'add' appends here are safe without that guard - see NOTES.md.",
  "ops": [
